ke the chief justice not  presiding over the event but that is  that's a frivolous issue that is uh most  the  vast consensus is that that is fine in  this case it's a former president not  the president  and so we're there's they're going to  try to distract with  issues related to perhaps some what  about is unlike other  other times when democrats or others  have tried to have said things that were  probably  not the same david quickly we've  mentioned it's a political trial could  it at some point be a criminal trial  uh yes this is not an uh either or there  could absolutely be criminal charges the  prosecution of a former president is not  something that a prosecutor will take up  on a whim though  they're going to look at this very very  carefully over time and in fact you  heard the president's lawyers suggest  that the proper remedy for this  it was a little bit odd to hear them say  this is a criminal prosecution of the  former president  all right david becker thank you very  much and we will bring you our coverage  of day three of the historic second  impeachment trial  of former president trump in a cbs news  special report we expect the senate to  begin around noon eastern  that would be 9 a.m pacific
 

